All existing tests pass. The `rename` function is implemented and compiles cleanly.

**What was added** (`src/store.rs`):

```rust
pub fn rename(dir: &Path, old_id: &str, new_id: &str, new_title: &str) -> std::io::Result<()>
```

**How it works:**
1. Reads the old `.note` file (`{old_id}.note`)
2. Splits on `\n---\n` into 4 parts (id, title, pinned, body)
3. Validates the file has 4 parts (returns error if malformed)
4. Writes a new file `{new_id}.note` with the new id and title, preserving the pinned flag and body
5. Deletes the old file

After calling `rename`, `load_all(dir)` returns exactly one note with the new id and title, and no trace remains under the old id.


